    '|a||So the reform didn''t make anyone a better farmer. It gave them back the last sack.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:cb54rq'
    '|b||That''s the theory. But in 1979 a lot more changed than who kept the last sack.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||The state raised what it paid for quota grain by about a fifth, and the bonus for grain sold above the quota from thirty to fifty percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:g4wy4y'
    '|b||Farmers were spreading more fertiliser too: over a third more nitrogen per hectare by 1984.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:14oizn4'
    '|a||And the first villages to switch weren''t chosen at random. They were poor places like Xiaogang, where the teams had done worst.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:fzv7l'
    '|a||The economist Justin Lin used timing to pull these apart. Provinces switched to household farming in different years; the price rises hit them all at once.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1mr8bts'
    '|a||Comparing early and late switchers, he credited the household system with about half the growth from 1978 to 1984.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:sl695j'
    '|b||Another study, by McMillan, Whalley and Zhu, gave it about three-quarters of the gain in productivity.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:9xpvvy'
    '|a||Now look past 1984. The harvest dropped, and stayed below its 1984 peak for four years.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1co84m9'
    '|b||That fits the story. Handing back the last sack is a one-time jump to a higher level, not a faster growth rate forever.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:t6id1'
    '|a||How sure are we? That the household system raised output a lot: mostly agreed. How much, against prices and fertiliser: contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:z1fiqr'
    '|b||And what it proves is narrow. The land stayed collective, and the quota was still sold at state prices. It shows what''s lost when nobody keeps the last sack, not that markets fix everything.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1abzzye'
    '|a||Three new cases. Vietnam gave farm households land contracts in 1988 and exported rice in 1989, after two decades as a net importer. What does that show on its own?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ql43db'
    '|a||It fits, but on its own it can''t separate the contracts from everything else that changed at the same time.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Two fishing boats. On one, the crew splits half the value of the catch; on the other, each deckhand gets a flat day wage. Which crew keeps hunting for fish late on a slow day?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||The share crew: every extra fish puts money in their pockets, while the day wage pays the same whatever the hold holds.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||A car-glass firm switched from hourly pay to pay per windscreen, and output per worker rose 44%. About half of the rise came from who joined and who stayed. What does the 44% measure?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13200
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Harder work plus a different workforce: about half is the same people working harder, the rest who joined and who stayed.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9280
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So what happened when markets were allowed in? Families got the last sack back, and the grain followed. Whether a failing market or a failing state costs more is the next fight.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12680
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||What did it take to pull China''s contracts apart from its price rises? Timing that varied by place: here, it fits, but the other changes must be checked.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Who gets anything from the last fish? Only those paid by the catch: here, the share crew.':
